# The build context for deploy/container/Dockerfile, which compiles `anistream-store` from the
# Cargo workspace. Cargo reads every member's manifest (crates/*) even to build one package, and
# crates read wit/ and assets/ at compile time, so those stay. The rest is left out to keep the
# context small, and so that editing the website or the docs does not invalidate the build.

# Build output. target/ alone runs to tens of gigabytes on a working machine.
**/target
# Other toolchains' dependencies, such as the admin page's under crates/anistream-store-core.
**/node_modules

# Version control, CI, editor and agent state.
.git
.github
.claude
**/.DS_Store

# Separate builds, outside the workspace: plugins are excluded from it in Cargo.toml, and the
# website and the deploy templates have their own toolchains.
plugins
website
deploy

# Prose, packaging and platform templates nothing compiles.
docs
packaging
tools
!tools/i18n
/README.md
/app.json
/fly.toml
/heroku.yml
/render.yaml

# README screenshots and local runtime files. assets/icon and assets/shaders stay: the app's
# crates include them.
/assets/*.png
/mpv-shot*
/anistream.db*
/.anistream
